{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1087825-h-tr-rule-clarification","id":1087825,"title":"H:tR Rule Clarification","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-04T11:33:27-07:00","id":1087825,"title":"H:tR Rule Clarification","content":"In combat, let's say you have players 1 through 5 attacking player 6. At the resolution stage, does player 6 make five separate soak rolls for each attack he or she sustains or one soak roll for the entire amount of damage inflicted? Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13102-driver_85","name":"driver_85","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T12:26:26-07:00","id":1087854,"title":"","content":"You soak each individual attack. There is no actual limit on how many attacks you might actually soak per turn. However, remember most hunters can only soak bashing damage and armor breaks down, if the damage of the attack is more than twice its armor rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}